# Scripted events for the "dips" recording (dips on single notes, then on chords), in ms on the
# recording's clock. With the settings export's switch assignments (Switch 2 and the right footswitch
# Transpose Up, the left footswitch Transpose Down), the first part transposes while notes are held,
# and returns to no transposition. The second part makes the left footswitch a sustain pedal through
# microLinn's NRPN importing, holds it across the chord dips, and puts things back.

48500   switch 2 150         # Switch 2: Transpose Up, a note held (47.85-54.6 s)
82000   pedal right down     # Transpose Up, a note held (81.15-86 s)
82300   pedal right up
130500  pedal left down      # Transpose Down, twice: back to no transposition (a note held, 129.65-136.6 s)
130800  pedal left up
131500  pedal left down
131800  pedal left up

200000  set importing 1
200100  nrpn 230 2           # Global Foot Left Assignment: Sustain
206000  pedal left down      # three or more notes held (205.25-209.1 s)
216000  pedal left up        # three or more notes held (214.35-218 s)
219000  midi B0 63 01 B0 62 66 B0 06 00 B0 26 12   # NRPN 230 = 18: the left footswitch back to Transpose Down
219100  set importing 0
